SECTION 11: FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS (FAQs)
======================================================================================

Q: Does my military foreign language training count toward the biblical language prerequisite?
A: No. Military Arabic, Farsi, Pashto, etc. do NOT substitute for Biblical Hebrew 
or Greek. However, your DLPT scores demonstrate language-learning ability and may 
help you succeed in biblical languages.

Q: Does my deployment count as missionary field experience?
A: Partially. Your deployment demonstrates cross-cultural adaptability and hardship 
endurance. However, you must ALSO complete missionary field experience under a 
career missionary to prove calling to Gospel ministry.

Q: Can I use my GI Bill at Berean if I'm still active duty?
A: Yes, if you are participating in the Active Duty GI Bill program. Contact our 
Veterans Certifying Official for details.

Q: What if I've already used some of my GI Bill benefits?
A: As long as you have at least 36 months remaining, you can complete Berean's 
3-year program. If you have less than 36 months, contact us to discuss options.

Q: Can my spouse use transferred GI Bill benefits at Berean?
A: Yes, if you transferred your benefits while on active duty. Your spouse would 
need to meet all admission prerequisites (including biblical language proficiency).

Q: Are you approved for Yellow Ribbon?
A: Yes, Berean participates in the Yellow Ribbon Program for eligible veterans, 
covering any tuition costs that exceed the GI Bill cap.

Q: What if I have a service-connected disability?
A: If you qualify for Vocational Rehabilitation & Employment (VR&E / Chapter 31), 
you may use those benefits at Berean. Contact our SCO for assistance.

Q: Do I need to be honorably discharged?
A: Yes. General discharge under honorable conditions may also qualify, but 
dishonorable or bad conduct discharges are not eligible for GI Bill benefits.

Q: When does the Monthly Housing Allowance get paid?
A: MHA is paid directly to you by the VA at the end of each month while classes 
are in session. First payment typically arrives 4-6 weeks after term starts.

Q: Does the GI Bill cover summer terms?
A: Berean operates year-round, so you will use GI Bill benefits continuously for 
all three years. This is actually advantageous because you receive housing 
allowance year-round.

